  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>tarlatamab</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01FX33</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Kong S et al. 2025</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>patients with previously treated small cell lung cancer</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>tarlatamab</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_tarlatamab/Tarlatamab_Kong2025_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Tarlatamab clearance (CL)</td><td>0.649</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>central volume of distribution (VC)</td><td>3.44</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>model-estimated median terminal phase elimination half-life</td><td>11.2</td><td>days</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr></table><h4>About tarlatamab</h4><p>Tarlatamab is a bispecific monoclonal antibody used to treat small cell lung cancer. It is an approved anticancer medicine and is authorised in the European Union, with further uses still under investigation.</p><p><small><b>Unverified</b> — written by glm-5.3-flash from general knowledge (no Wikidata entry found) and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Tarlatamab\">Tarlatamab</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Kong S et al. (2025). Population Pharmacokinetics of Tarlatamab, a Half-Life Extended DLL3-Directed Bispecific T-Cell Engager in Patients with Previously Treated Small Cell Lung Cancer. <i>Clinical pharmacokinetics 64(5):729–741</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40262-025-01499-z\">10.1007/s40262-025-01499-z</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40261494\">40261494</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Kong_2025: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
